From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:18:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] usb_canbus: Restart interrupted stall deadlines

Shutdown removes all scheduler timers before invoking the shutdown
callbacks.  If the bridge is waiting for transmit capacity at that
point, it retains BSS_BLOCKING without a timer to expire the wait.  A
controller that remains full can then block the host queue indefinitely,
including messages intended for the local bridge MCU.

Reset a blocked wait to BSS_READY in usb_shutdown().  The existing task
wakeup retries the pending frame and arms a fresh 50ms deadline if the
controller is still full.  Preserve an already reported discard state
so recovery notifications remain paired.  CAN framing is unchanged.

A native fault-injection harness reproduces the missing deadline before
this change and passes afterwards.  It also checks timeout discards,
recovery notifications, and successful cancellation when capacity
returns.  The RP2040 USB-CAN firmware build passes.

Signed-off-by: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 86df7533c0bce3396de4b0535d384616f796a65e)

diff --git a/src/generic/usb_canbus.c b/src/generic/usb_canbus.c
index ab1f59ce..a355de18 100644
--- a/src/generic/usb_canbus.c
+++ b/src/generic/usb_canbus.c
@@ -995,6 +995,11 @@ DECL_TASK(usb_ep0_task);
 void
 usb_shutdown(void)
 {
+    // Shutdown removed the stall timer; let the task arm a new deadline.
+    if (UsbCan.bus_send_state == BSS_BLOCKING) {
+        UsbCan.bus_send_state = BSS_READY;
+        writeb(&UsbCan.bus_send_timed_out, 0);
+    }
     wake_usbcan_task();
     usb_notify_ep0();
 }
